    <p class="hero__tagline" style="font-size: 1.35rem;">A book with several nervous systems.</p>
    <div class="content-section__body">
      <p>
        I write poems of the moment something appears unsaid, politely avoided,
        scientifically misunderstood, emotionally falsified or too funny not to put
        under pressure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="content-section__body"><strong>FEED</strong> moves between several recurring territories:</p>
    <ul class="poetry-territories fact-list">
      <li>Science, physics and empirical reality</li>
      <li>Life poems, often at their least polite</li>
      <li>Compressed aphoristic pieces</li>
      <li>Geopolitical snapshots</li>
      <li>Art, artists and the machinery around art</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="content-section__heading">About the manuscript</h2>
    <div class="content-section__body">
      <p>
        <strong>FEED</strong> is a selected collection of approximately
        {{ current_work.poem_count_approx }} poems drawn from a much larger body of work.
      </p>
      <p>
        The register moves from brutal to tender, from empirical to obscene, from the
        one-line cut to the long-form argument. The point is the same consciousness
        looking at different kinds of reality without pretending they belong to
        different universes.
      </p>
      <p>Some poems explain.</p>
      <p>Some accuse.</p>
      <p>Some remember.</p>
      <p>Some laugh at precisely the wrong moment.</p>
      <p>A few do all four.</p>
      <p><strong>Status:</strong> {{ current_work.poetry_status }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

